.TH M4 1 "FUZIX" "Ripple"
.SH NAME
m4 \- expand text macros
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B m4 [file ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read files or standard input and expand macros. The default quote characters
are the backtick and apostrophe. Arguments are enclosed in parentheses;
macro definitions substitute $1 through $9.
.PP
Builtins include define, undefine, ifdef, ifelse, changequote, dnl, include,
sinclude, divert, undivert, divnum, dumpdef, errprint, eval, incr, decr,
index, len, substr, translit and syscmd. This is the small MWC implementation;
GNU options such as -D, -I and -P and GNU-specific builtins are not present.
.PP
Diversions 1 through 9 use unlinked temporary files. divert(0) returns to
standard output, and undivert copies saved output without re-expanding it.
A negative diversion discards output. Expansion/input nesting is bounded;
allocation failures and incomplete calls or quotes report errors.
.PP
Eval uses signed 32-bit integer arithmetic. Its arithmetic operators include
+, -, *, /, %, exponentiation, comparisons, !, &, and |. Division by zero
reports an error. This evaluator does not promise arbitrary precision.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
define(`greet',`Hello, $1!')dnl
greet(`Ripple')
.fi
